## Why This Is Asked

Assesses practical E2E skills: gating UX with feature flags, deterministic tests, data seeding, and test isolation using Cypress or Playwright.

## Key Concepts

- Feature flags and gating
- Test data seeding per run
- LocalStorage state as idempotence marker
- Network/mocks to deterministically simulate flag responses
- Time-bounded execution for beginner scenarios

## Code Example

```javascript
// Playwright skeleton
test('onboarding respects flag', async ({ page }) => {
  await page.route('**/flags**', r => r.fulfill({ status: 200, body: JSON.stringify({ onboarding: true }) }));
  await page.goto('https://app.local/');
  await expect(page.locator('#onboard-modal')).toBeVisible();
  await page.locator('#finish').click();
  const stored = await page.evaluate(() => localStorage.getItem('onboarding_complete'));
  expect(stored).toBe('true');
  await page.reload();
  await expect(page.locator('#onboard-modal')).toBeHidden();
});
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you extend this to multi-tenant setups with per-tenant flag overrides?
- How would you ensure the test remains reliable when the flag toggles during a session?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests involving asynchronous exports and email notifications are common in SaaS applications. This question evaluates practical familiarity with end-to-end testing flows, mocking external services, and ensuring idempotency under rapid repeated actions.

## Key Concepts

- Asynchronous job orchestration and eventual consistency
- Mocking external services (export service and email delivery)
- Test data isolation and seeding
- Idempotency and race condition handling

## Code Example

```javascript
import { test, expect } from '@playwright/test';

test('data export flow is idempotent', async ({ page }) => {
  await page.goto('/dashboard');

  await seedTestData({ userId: 'user-123', dataset: [...] });

  await page.fill('#date-from', '2024-01-01');
  await page.fill('#date-to', '2024-01-31');
  await page.selectOption('#status', 'completed');

  await page.click('#export-btn');

  await page.route('**/api/export', async (route) => {
    await route.fulfill({ status: 200, body: { jobId: 'job-123', status: 'completed' } });
  });

  await page.route('**/api/email/send', async (route) => {
    await route.fulfill({ status: 200 });
  });

  await expect(page.locator('#download-link')).toBeVisible({ timeout: 10000 });

  const emailRequests = [];
  await page.on('request', (req) => {
    if (req.url().includes('/api/email/send')) {
      emailRequests.push(req);
    }
  });

  await page.click('#export-btn');
  await page.waitForTimeout(500);

  expect(emailRequests).toHaveLength(1);
});
```

